\section{Enterprise Cluster Stress Testing and Stability Verification}
This appendix documents the full-system stress testing performed on the
real-time genetic blueprint simulation architecture deployed on a 64-node
NVIDIA HGX H100 cluster. The objective is to validate numerical resilience,
zero-copy buffer integrity, and Lyapunov-governed stability under extreme
burst telemetry and forced manifold strain.

\subsection{Stress Testing Environment}
All tests were executed on a synchronized CUDA fabric with direct-to-chip
liquid cooling. Each node contains 8$\times$H100 GPUs connected through
NVLink 4.0, with unified ring-buffer ingestion and real-time telemetry
monitoring.

